    "The finance ministry costs the sixty-thousand allowance at 48 billion złoty";
!}

= February 2024 — Forty-eight billion, and a volunteer wanted

**Andrzej Domański**, Minister of Finance, circulates the costing for konkret
number four. Raising the tax-free allowance from thirty thousand złoty to
sixty thousand removes roughly forty-eight billion złoty a year from personal
income tax. It is the single most expensive promise on the list, it was
repeated in every campaign hall, and there is no version of the 2024 budget
that contains it.

The politics are worse than the arithmetic. The allowance is worth most to
people who earn enough to use all of it, which is why it was never our
promise; it was, however, understood by pensioners and by the self-employed as
money already granted. And it cannot simply be dropped, because dropping it is
the first unambiguous broken promise of the term.

So the search begins for somebody else to drop it. Poland 2050 has already
said in private that it does not support the full allowance. PSL offers a way
out with its name on it: a ladder, five thousand more this year, ten the next,
fifteen after that, sixty by the end of the term. The Chancellery likes the
ladder and likes even better the idea that [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "psl": a partner?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and
government_party != "psl": an opposition party?] announces it.

[? if konkrety_answer = "Built the delivery scoreboard": The delivery
committee's February table has konkret four in the blocking column with the
finance ministry's name in it, which is not the name anybody expected to find
there.?]
[? if konkrety_answer = "Shielded the government": We spent January explaining
that the pace was reasonable. That performance is being cited to us now as a
reason to explain this too.?]
[? if konkrety_answer = "Demanded names": We spent January demanding that KO
name a partner. This is the offer to become one voluntarily.?]
[? if pension_defence_credit >= 4: We answered the pension questions in the
2023 referendum instead of boycotting them, and the costed position we built
then is the only reason our objection to this allowance is heard as economics
rather than as envy.?]
[? if fiscal_stress >= 25: The budget is already carrying more than it can,
which makes the argument easier to win and the announcement harder to
survive.?]

- @kwota_kill
- @kwota_swap
- @kwota_ladder
- @kwota_alibi
- @kwota_quiet

@kwota_kill
title: Say plainly that it is a bad promise and the money belongs in services
subtitle: The honest answer and the one that puts our face on the broken promise; buys standing with public-service workers and hands KO a volunteer.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna = "Killed openly by the Left";
Q.labor_credibility += 5;
Q.public_sector_support += 5;
Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
Q.institutional_trust += 3;
Q.fiscal_stress = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.fiscal_stress) || 0) - 4);
Q.public_trust -= 3;
Q.household_security -= 2;
Q.ko_relation += 4;
Q.pensioner_support -= 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.1;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 5;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 6;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left says the sixty-thousand allowance is a bad promise and should not be kept";
!}

We say it in the chamber and we say it with the numbers. Forty-eight billion
złoty is four years of the hospital debt, or the whole social housing
programme that nobody has funded since 2007, or a real pay settlement for the
people who kept the schools open. It should not be spent making the tax system
flatter.

It is the correct position and it is received the way correct positions
usually are. The clip that travels is a Left politician explaining why a tax
cut is not being delivered, and the audience for that clip includes every
pensioner who was told in September that the money was coming.

The Chancellery is delighted. Konkret four now has a named executioner, and
the name is not Tusk's.

- @poland_event_queue: Say it plainly

@kwota_swap
title: Demand the forty-eight billion back as progressive financing
subtitle: Requires the 2023 referendum record. Kills the allowance and charges for it: a capital-income bracket and a costed social floor in the same statement.
choose-if: pension_defence_credit >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: We have no costed pension and tax record from 2023 to put behind a counter-proposal, so a demand of this size would be read as a slogan.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna = "Traded for progressive financing";
Q.konkrety_left_items += 1;
Q.konkrety_left_credit += 1;
Q.labor_credibility += 6;
Q.public_sector_support += 4;
Q.pensioner_support += 3;
Q.household_security += 3;
Q.progressive_credibility += 4;
Q.issue_ownership += 4;
Q.negotiation_capital += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.fiscal_stress = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.fiscal_stress) || 0) - 2);
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.15;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 8;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 5;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 9;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left kills the flat allowance and demands a capital-income bracket instead";
!}

We agree that konkret four dies, and we attach a price to agreeing. The
statement is one page: the allowance is withdrawn, a bracket on capital income
replaces part of the revenue, and the difference is committed in writing to the
health service and to the widow's pension we have been carrying since the
autumn.

Because we answered the referendum on pensions rather than refusing it, the
costings we published in 2023 are already in circulation and the press treats
this as a fiscal position rather than as a demand. Domański's officials confirm
the arithmetic works, in the tone of officials who wish it did not.

KO wanted a partner to hold the knife. It has one, holding an invoice.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the invoice

@kwota_ladder
title: Take PSL's ladder and bank the first step
subtitle: Requires a workable relationship with PSL. Nobody breaks a promise and nobody keeps one; only a PSL cabinet place makes this a coalition settlement.
choose-if: psl_relation >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: Relations with PSL are too poor for a joint announcement; the ladder would be presented as theirs alone.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna = "Staged ladder agreed with PSL";
Q.psl_relation += 7;
if (Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet || Q.government_party == "psl") {
    Q.psl_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 5
    );
}
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 3
);
Q.household_security += 3;
Q.rural_support += 2;
Q.fiscal_stress += 3;
Q.budget_promises += 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.coalition_blur += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline = Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet || Q.government_party == "psl"
    ? "The coalition converts the sixty-thousand allowance into a four-year ladder"
    : "KO and opposition PSL convert the allowance into a four-year ladder";
!}

We take the ladder. Five thousand this year, and a schedule in the coalition
minutes for the rest[? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party =
"psl": , signed by PSL as a cabinet party?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0
and government_party != "psl": ; PSL endorses it from opposition but cannot
bind the cabinet?], which means the promise is not broken so much as lengthened
past the point where anybody will still be checking.

PSL gets the announcement, which is what PSL wanted, and stops treating us as
the party that costs it money. The Chancellery gets a headline containing the
words *tax-free allowance* and *rises*. The self-employed voter who was
promised sixty thousand gets five.

It is the most professional thing to do in February and it is the reason the
word *konkret* will be used sarcastically by December.

- @poland_event_queue: Bank the first step

@kwota_alibi
title: Refuse to be the alibi and make KO bury its own promise
subtitle: Requires the December annex. Costs the coalition a fortnight and forces the party that made the promise to be the party that withdraws it.
choose-if: konkrety_receipts = 1
unavailable-subtitle: With nothing in writing from December, refusing to carry the retreat is a matter of our word against the Chancellery's.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna = "Left refused to carry KO's retreat";
Q.konkrety_ownership = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.konkrety_ownership) || 0) - 15
);
Q.media_capacity += 4;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.institutional_trust += 2;
Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 8;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 7;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left refuses to announce the withdrawal of a promise it never made";
!}

The answer goes back on paper, and the paper is the annex we filed in December.
Konkret four is not in our column. It was never in our column. If it is being
withdrawn, the withdrawal will be announced by the ministry holding it and the
party that promised it, on camera, in its own words.

The Chancellery spends ten days looking for another volunteer and does not find
one, because PSL has read our annex and copied the manoeuvre. Eventually
Domański does it himself, flanked by nobody, and the phrase *the government
has decided not to proceed this year* enters the record with a single party's
name attached.

Tusk does not forgive this. He is also aware that we have simply declined to
lie for him, which makes the grievance difficult to voice out loud.

- @poland_event_queue: Send it back to its author

@kwota_quiet
title: Let it die quietly and say nothing at all
subtitle: Spends nothing this month; the promise decays without an author, and in March the story is written by whoever does have a quote.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna = "Allowed to lapse without comment";
Q.public_trust -= 2;
Q.media_capacity -= 1;
Q.movement_autonomy = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) - 2);
Q.coalition_blur += 3;
Q.ko_relation += 1;
Q.pis_poll_momentum += 0.1;
Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The sixty-thousand allowance disappears from the government's plans without an announcement";
!}

We do not comment. The costing stops being circulated, the promise stops being
mentioned in ministerial interviews, and by the end of the month it has moved
from *this year* to *this term* to nothing at all, without any single day on
which it was withdrawn.

This is the cheapest February available and it is not free. A promise that dies
without an author is inherited by the opposition, which has been waiting for
precisely one unambiguous example and now has the most expensive one on the
list, undefended.

Konfederacja's tax people put it on a graphic within the week. It is a good
graphic.

- @poland_event_queue: Let it lapse
